  <h2 id="stages">The four stages of a redemption</h2>
  <p>Every redemption moves through the same four stages. The published number from an operator usually covers only one of them, which is why real wait times run longer than the marketing figure.</p>
  <ul class="tick-list">
    <li><b>Request.</b> You submit the redemption. The operator checks your Sweeps Coins balance, playthrough completion and any daily caps.</li>
    <li><b>Verification (KYC).</b> First redemptions trigger a document check: government ID, proof of address, and sometimes the payment method itself. This is the stage that adds days.</li>
    <li><b>Processing.</b> The operator approves and releases the payment internally. Pulsz and McLuck both state this can take up to 72 hours.</li>
    <li><b>Delivery.</b> The payment network moves the money. Crypto settles fastest; bank transfers depend on banking days.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="first-vs-repeat">First redemption vs repeat redemption</h2>
  <p>The single largest variable is whether your account is already verified. A first redemption carries the full KYC check; later redemptions from the same verified account skip most of it. Pulsz makes this explicit by quoting 3 to 7 business days for a first redemption and shorter handling thereafter. When you compare operators, compare like for like: either all first redemptions or all repeat redemptions.</p>

  <h2 id="delays">Why redemptions get delayed</h2>
  <ul class="tick-list">
    <li class="bad"><b>Identity mismatch.</b> The name or address on your ID does not match the account, or the payment method is in a different name.</li>
    <li class="bad"><b>Incomplete wagering.</b> Sweeps Coins must be played through before redemption; WOW Vegas raised its requirement from 0.1x to 1x in February 2025.</li>
    <li class="bad"><b>Weekend and holiday timing.</b> Bank transfers settle on banking days, so a Friday request can sit until the following week.</li>
    <li class="bad"><b>Caps and thresholds.</b> McLuck caps redemptions at 10,000 SC per day (4,900 SC in Florida and New York) and enforces minimums of 75 SC for bank transfer and 10 SC for gift cards.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="troubleshooting">Pending redemption troubleshooting</h2>
  <p>If a redemption sits in a pending state, work through this order before contacting support:</p>
  <ul class="tick-list">
    <li class="good"><b>Check verification status.</b> If the operator has requested documents, nothing moves until they are approved. Upload clear, current documents that match your account details exactly.</li>
    <li class="good"><b>Confirm wagering completion.</b> Check that all Sweeps Coins in the request have met the playthrough requirement.</li>
    <li class="good"><b>Check the minimum.</b> Requests below the operator minimum (for example 40 SC at Stake.us or 75 SC for a McLuck bank transfer) will not process.</li>
    <li class="good"><b>Count banking days, not calendar days.</b> A "2-5 day" bank transfer means banking days for the delivery stage.</li>
    <li class="good"><b>Then contact support.</b> Ask for the specific stage your redemption is in: verification, processing or delivery. The answer tells you whether the hold-up is yours to fix or theirs.</li>
  </ul>

